//
// H8, the reproduction gate: air-fuse-pipeline-launches given J7a's three
// stages as SEPARATE attributed air.launch ops must produce the module
// builders/norm_tail.py writes BY HAND -- the one that is gated, measured
// (mean_rel_L1 3.620e-3) and known to route.
//
// WHY REPRODUCTION IS THE DELIVERABLE AND NOT "IT EMITTED A FUSED MODULE"
// R1 -- the one hand-built instance of this composition (J7a x2 + J7b) -- is
// correct only at the fully degenerate rung and carries two distinct open
// hardware defects (README queue items 21 and 23), while the module-
// interpreting arm certifies it element-exact at all 11 ladder shapes. So a
// pass that can GENERATE these compositions generates instances of a shape not
// yet known to work, and "the pass emitted plausible IR" would be exactly the
// kind of check this project has four times found could not fail. What is
// gated here is bounded and checkable: the pass reproduces a KNOWN-GOOD
// reference, and refuses malformed input.
//
// WHY BYTE EQUALITY RATHER THAN A LIST OF STRUCTURAL RESEMBLANCES
// A structural comparison is only as good as the list of things it names, and
// doc 23 section 5 records the list missing the phase's own claim (a check
// counting packet typing could not see an edge round-tripping through L3).
// Byte equality of the printed module needs no list: it implies equality on
// every axis such a check could name and on every axis it could forget, and --
// aircc being deterministic -- it implies the ROUTED designs are identical
// without compiling either. Both sides are printed by the same air-opt, so the
// comparison cannot turn on printer differences.
//
// WHY THE UNFUSED FORM IS THE SAME BUILDER
// build_norm_tail_module(stage_launches=True) emits the same three herd bodies
// as the default arrangement, differing only in launch/segment nesting. Were
// it a separate transcription this gate would compare two pieces of Python
// rather than test the pass. Verified separately: the DEFAULT arrangement's IR
// is byte-identical to the pre-H8 builder's, so J7a's own gate does not move.
//
// This arm needs an air-opt carrying the pass and nothing else -- no NPU, no
// Peano, no kernel objects, no device lock. A tree predating the pass reports
// UNSUPPORTED rather than failing, and that does NOT weaken coverage of the
// pass itself: its existence and behaviour are pinned unconditionally by
// mlir/test/Transform/AIRFusePipelineLaunches/*.mlir in check-air-mlir. What
// this feature guards is only the builder-level reproduction gate, which can
// say nothing at all without a matching binary.
//
// Editing this header: lit scans the WHOLE file for directives, so naming one
// in prose registers as a second directive. Describe them, never spell them out.
//
// REQUIRES: air_fuse_pipeline_launches
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_pipeline_fusion
// RUN: cd test_pipeline_fusion
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile check-pipeline-fusion | FileCheck %s
//
// The provenance line first: which binary answered. A gate that silently ran
// an air-opt without the pass would fail every comparison for the wrong reason,
// so the script refuses that case explicitly rather than reporting differences.
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] air-opt:
//
// THE REPRODUCTION CLAUSE, per shape and variant. The byte count is in the
// verdict so a comparison that succeeded against an empty or truncated module
// cannot match here, and the launch/segment/herd counts are too -- 3 launches
// and 3 segments IN is what says the gate was not comparing the reference to
// itself, and 1 launch / 1 segment / 3 herds OUT is the operation itself
// (residency holds only within a segment).
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 128x768: REPRODUCED (3 launches/3 segments in -> 1 launch/1 segment/3 herds out, {{[0-9]+}} bytes byte-identical to the hand-written module)
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 128x768 plane_major: REPRODUCED (3 launches/3 segments in -> 1 launch/1 segment/3 herds out, {{[0-9]+}} bytes byte-identical to the hand-written module)
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 128x768 plane_major+mirror_out: REPRODUCED (3 launches/3 segments in -> 1 launch/1 segment/3 herds out, {{[0-9]+}} bytes byte-identical to the hand-written module)
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 4096x768: REPRODUCED (3 launches/3 segments in -> 1 launch/1 segment/3 herds out, {{[0-9]+}} bytes byte-identical to the hand-written module)
//
// The two skips are matched, not tolerated: plane_major at 4096 rows exceeds
// the shim BD stride cap and the BUILDER refuses it (see builders/norm_tail.py).
// Matching the line is what stops a shape silently disappearing from the gate.
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 4096x768 plane_major: SKIPPED
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 4096x768 plane_major+mirror_out: SKIPPED
//
// J7b, where it applies: ffn_accum is ONE stage, so fusing its group must be an
// IDENTITY. Not a degenerate case worth skipping -- it is the clause that says
// the pass leaves the compiler-formed accumulator ring and the memtile A|B feed
// untouched, and it is where the air.staging = "accum_in_place" claim is
// checked against the IR rather than carried.
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] ffn_accum 1-stage group: IDENTITY (accum_in_place claim accepted, module byte-unchanged)
//
// THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS, matched individually because an arm that cannot fail
// is not a gate. Declining to fuse is NOT a safe fallback here: the stages stay
// in separate air.launch ops, each lowers to its own aie.device, and the
// declared L1->L1 edges span them -- doc 23's refuse-versus-skip discriminator,
// the same one that makes air-fuse-packet-put-loops' silence wrong. The first
// two are derived by rewriting the real builder's output, so they cannot drift
// away from what the builder emits.
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] negative control: duplicate stage index: REFUSED
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] negative control: gap in stage indices: REFUSED
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] negative control: accum_in_place claim without the ring shape: REFUSED
//
// The routed clause last: fusing N stages into one segment ADDS their
// per-column L3-facing demand (doc 23's rule, per column ACROSS stacked herds),
// which is the constraint fusion itself creates. Counted with
// ffn_resident_structure's census, not a third counter. One aie.device is the
// point of the exercise; 16 core-to-core flows are the two inter-stage edges,
// one per column each.
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] norm_tail 128x768 fused: ROUTED (1 aie.device, 16 L1->L1 flows, worst column 2/2 shim MM2S)
// CHECK: [pipeline-fusion] PASS
